6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.09132197371681874,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":0.06409782335742573,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":32.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":3.3980003576771245,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.028995564751956943,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":23.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.5675733630172142,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0010545687703673466,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":1.1,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03500121204587399,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":50.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.009358089318462381,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":38.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0063987427031881455,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.0047400002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ovintiv Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an oil and natural gas exploration and production company in North America. The company operates through USA Operations and Canadian Operations segments. It is involved in the exploration, development, production, and marketing of oil, NGLs, natural gas and other related activities in the Permian in West Texas and Anadarko in West-central Oklahoma in the United States, as well as in the Montney in northwest Alberta and northeast British Columbia. The company was formerly known as Encana Corporation and changed its name to Ovintiv Inc. in January 2020. Ovintiv Inc. was incorporated in 2020 and is based in Denver, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brendan Michael McCracken | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $6.1M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers. Each employee generates $1.0M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $39K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Ovintiv Inc. (DE) is a large-cap energy business with a $17.6B market cap on $8.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 8% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $1.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.94\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 31% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 40% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","23 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Energy peers","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Is Ovintiv (NYSE:OVV) Gaining Attention Across Energy Markets?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/energy/why-is-ovintiv-nyseovv-gaining-attention-across-energy-markets","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577860.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.847,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(OVV) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktrad